00:11:55.840 --> 00:12:00.240
A word of advice; even though these playlists&nbsp;
are divided based on your Voltaic rank,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:00.240 --> 00:12:04.160
they are not “easy” playlists. I made them&nbsp;
with the intention for you to be challenged&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:04.160 --> 00:12:07.680
through the whole playthrough, because I&nbsp;
firmly believe that frustration is key for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:07.680 --> 00:12:12.720
fast improvement when learning new skills, and&nbsp;
using scenarios that feel too easy for you is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:12.720 --> 00:12:18.320
really not optimal for improvement. So if you&nbsp;
feel that the scenarios are hard, that is ok,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:18.880 --> 00:12:23.280
and if you get frustrated that is ok too!&nbsp;
The important part is that you understand&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:23.280 --> 00:12:26.160
that you are getting frustrated because&nbsp;
you are trying to overcome the current&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:26.160 --> 00:12:30.080
limitations of your aiming ability and you&nbsp;
have to push through the whole playlist.

00:12:31.120 --> 00:12:37.840
So, the takeaway, is that getting frustrated is&nbsp;
ok, but quitting because of frustration isn’t.

00:12:37.840 --> 00:12:38.391
